I am sitting in the museum's café and taking a break.
I drink a cup of coffee and relax.
I take the blue plates out of my bag.
These plates fit perfectly in my kitchen.
I take a picture of them with my phone.
I send the picture to my sister, Sofía.
"Just look at these beautiful plates," I write.
"I found them at a market an hour ago."
Sofía answers me almost immediately.
She sends an old picture back to me.
This message makes me very happy.
The picture shows the two of us at a large flea market in Mexico.
"Do you remember this market?"
Sofía asks in the next message.
"We were there exactly two years ago!" she writes.
I look at our happy faces in the picture.
It feels like a very long time ago.
Two years ago, I still lived in Mexico.
I smile and write a happy message back.
